 "about_text": "space Un is a Tokyo arts and culture venue focused on contemporary African art and cultural exchange between Japan and Africa. It was initiated by collector Edna Dumas, driven by her passion for contemporary African art and wish to support African artists, and co-founded with actor and artist Yuta Nakano. The gallery presents exhibitions of artists from the African continent and its diaspora, alongside cross-disciplinary programming including workshops, music events, film nights, and lectures. It also runs an invitation-only residency program linking artists' stays at Yoshino Cedar House in Nara with solo exhibitions in Tokyo. The gallery space in Minami-Aoyama was designed by architect Go Hasegawa, blending Japanese spatial sensibility with African heritage.",
